to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}$\n- $[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}$\n- $[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/assets/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140362/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "434a82c2-7964-525a-85b9-eb17fa7b5b26"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140362"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97066/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "2ab0abe7-e399-5e89-ae9f-f99fb59e7cae" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97066/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "b9295948-84fa-5a80-975c-3471f76227ca" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97066/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "241b9046-28c9-5910-89c0-56f8b1280904" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/i