B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to C}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/assets/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{C}.$ First, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 6 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 18 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-97111/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61bd0b4f-165c-5f31-b4ec-e0eff7e758e1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97111"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-38362"] :question/problem "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to this basis. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the basis $B$ and standard basis $S$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/assets/dbd020362f950fe8bfb4c592652b9e78a73610fa01a247b0b7ead6f201bf9ea5.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{S}={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1},\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 3-5\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{S} & ={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-140481/selection/93982b4353462b2451a54f2f3dfd2b545e659fa385224d54cf27308d79359a71" :answer/id #uuid "d94722c7-9faf-50a2-8b4b-46ccade623ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 10 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140481/selection/210064fea233c9ea6075064e1c88464d3149ce1f127b409ca9658923ccfcaa58" :answer/id #uuid "b320df15-eba9-5fb5-a3da-0823cad4a3d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & -9 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140481/selection/e5cf589c752735334d5de50a938858553911601eab58a9156cc80a57f83b7530" :answer/id #uuid "45f750d5-9018-54f5-b733-6f4ef0057a55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 10 \\\\ -6 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140481/selection/fe91db9f883ea7fba182439ce4172478b2fe17a0c68785817c89a34cce90a9c8" :answer/id #uuid "4ee7f521-70f7-5566-a4d9-da6f3aa6fa12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 7 \\\\ -9 & 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140481/selection/88817ba1c972a3699709aca64e200a47acf0d30836c0441b562d2afd13665bda" :answer/id #uuid "825d0da3-ad25-5cbb-85f0-24a80c26c7cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 7 \\\\ -6 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140481/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8602ac26-e81e-58e7-b48a-7b9b59f07e57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140481/selection/e5cf589c752735334d5de50a938858553911601eab58a9156cc80a57f83b7530" :answer-field/choices ["q-140481/selection/93982b4353462b2451a54f2f3dfd2b545e659fa385224d54cf27308d79359a71" "q-140481/selection/210064fea233c9ea6075064e1c88464d3149ce1f127b409ca9658923ccfcaa58" "q-140481/selection/e5cf589c752735334d5de50a938858553911601eab58a9156cc80a57f83b7530" "q-140481/selection/fe91db9f883ea7fba182439ce4172478b2fe17a0c68785817c89a34cce90a9c8" "q-140481/selection/88817ba1c972a3699709aca64e200a47acf0d30836c0441b562d2afd13665bda"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140481" :question/id #uuid "a4d35477-b857-55bc-8644-6d12a78d9e7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-140481" :question/problem "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to this basis. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the basis $B$ and standard basis $S$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/assets/dbd020362f950fe8bfb4c592652b9e78a73610fa01a247b0b7ead6f201bf9ea5.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{S}={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1},\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{S} & ={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -8 \\\\ -4 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 10 \\\\ -6 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-140481/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "969220db-a686-511b-b33a-0b4f6ab66b1a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140481"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97122/selection/7d3efa01508733a6aba194a7340d65c5f56c9e0e9815c7564cc733b215b86095" :answer/id #uuid "f5568fe6-e6ea-52e8-b0ae-4c923979060d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -23 & 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97122/selection/238fd4c63bb7671dd78e9fb512d91fdeecacd200e3760818c86bc410d9605223" :answer/id #uuid "1f1da4c9-3f20-5a3c-aaaa-b605a81eee4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97122/selection/03e7b8481fa5c15ca6c0bb81b1ae594810ca748faebd15370d423180946bc843" :answer/id #uuid "1d5419d7-3650-5809-8e32-6c6090b68653" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97122/selection/a45e47c382af05a4016f38b66bd65e8e50a1ba2d6843b4ee11e5d5623f8a5ad4" :answer/id #uuid "ce8ef583-ae84-5fcd-9843-0ff181bfea23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 23 & -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97122/selection/5b2055caa8f25744cf9797625dabff08cfc8e9d19fe8278356e60e71c6c52c7c" :answer/id #uuid "5820bd7f-e521-5c00-8402-6242a64b7fe9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 23 & -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97122/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d13d31e1-69d8-539b-8c8b-8ab9e5ea7ef1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97122/selection/7d3efa01508733a6aba194a7340d65c5f56c9e0e9815c7564cc733b215b86095" :answer-field/choices ["q-97122/selection/7d3efa01508733a6aba194a7340d65c5f56c9e0e9815c7564cc733b215b86095" "q-97122/selection/238fd4c63bb7671dd78e9fb512d91fdeecacd200e3760818c86bc410d9605223" "q-97122/selection/03e7b8481fa5c15ca6c0bb81b1ae594810ca748faebd15370d423180946bc843" "q-97122/selection/a45e47c382af05a4016f38b66bd65e8e50a1ba2d6843b4ee11e5d5623f8a5ad4" "q-97122/selection/5b2055caa8f25744cf9797625dabff08cfc8e9d19fe8278356e60e71c6c52c7c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97122" :question/id #uuid "fc7f6482-f87f-5b59-92e8-8de06bb91dfe" :question/math-academy-id "q-97122" :question/problem "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to this basis. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the basis $B$ and standard basis $S$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14067267/assets/dbd020362f950fe8bfb4c592652b9e78a73610fa01a247b0b7ead6f201bf9ea5.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{S}={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1},\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{S} & ={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -23 & 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97122/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "969220db-a686-511b-b33a-0b4f6ab66b1a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97122"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-38455/selection/a806de857a17e3027a574f3453d6b71e0773d2230383bcadc0a72f64106888d3" :answer/id #uuid "b3c71e03-0342-59f9-b535-55478d8c1262" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 5 \\\\ -8 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38455/selection/e718f0514b62ba7dde18ad336c17c925e5f397304559972a2002c3707265147a" :answer/id #uuid "ac822fbe-8fe7-5c0c-b9a3-bd9b2de450b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}11 & 8 \\\\ -10 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38455/selection/ff0b2b79a7153a94aecde6a10232b1ac3095d8d3c77296348124d4cab72324f4" :answer/id #uuid "bfb8c164-e160-535a-ab56-598186ce409c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 11 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38455/selection/52d588e5675a45c12804e49f4dd2678d2810fc578fbb1082eff0a4a40de56ecf" :answer/id #uuid "6d4de119-20b9-543b-8b26-82307b115ac4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -6