 matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{S}={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1},\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-4)\\cdot 4-3\\cdot (-5)}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{S} & ={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 & 8 \\\\ -10 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-38455/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "969220db-a686-511b-b33a-0b4f6ab66b1a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38455"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97119/selection/cb7ba7c2ae725977cc706b86da7c4bf3bdbb6759600df833233d05589da9ed8c" :answer/id #uuid "5ab341c1-fcc9-51ea-823c-b9945fc813e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97119/selection/c50f29a6e4c8a230d58d95517d2308a7da8fd5b3eba87e18512d96152e4447ab" :answer/id #uuid "94651103-b46c-5b71-a3bc-c0dd024faffa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97119/selection/13380af7f13931cd6d3a3b8877e0b47c2f